e sky, and said, “Abraham, Abraham!” He said, “Here I am.” He said, “Don’t lay your hand on the boy or do anything to him. For now I know that you fear God, since you have not withheld your son, your only son, from me.”","canonicalTextHash":"b83e7632f36ef622992997e66dfaa22f221ff1ac325de05665768ca8b874c0ea","citation":"Genesis 22:11–12","refId":"evidence:4881f25aaf201e32d03173b2","referenceHash":"4881f25aaf201e32d03173b2a009c70a01542551f5ec7f8238dcea620031c18a","sourceIds":["engwebu:gen:22:11-12"]},{"canonicalText":"who kept the law of the Most High, and was taken into covenant with him. In his flesh he established the covenant. When he was tested, he was found faithful.","canonicalTextHash":"acab34c16bf58fdfa9f0a4f6ffd59b4775b3107b7b39cc50056991f2d2b81753","citation":"Sirach 44:20","refId":"evidence:dc3109dea2cd975a91f48d31","referenceHash":"dc3109dea2cd975a91f48d31bba72c209ec4f3301eef9400a0cf003608673756","sourceIds":["engwebu:sir:44:20"]},{"canonicalText":"Wasn’t Abraham found faithful in temptation, and it was reckoned to him for righteousness?","canonicalTextHash":"214c574f091bb61a935f154a6f66bfa0ff647de1b126c19f7d78c40895fbf107","citation":"1 Maccabees 2:52","refId":"evidence:21051c9784f0885fd3c2fb43","referenceHash":"d7d7f3f8f9cf87cdac197685de423cbf5cafd16b4db99c71c1a0aa5516a35fab","sourceIds":["engwebu:1ma:2:52"]},{"canonicalText":"Wasn’t Abraham our father justified by works, in that he offered up Isaac his son on the altar? You see that faith worked with his works, and by works faith was perfected. So the Scripture was fulfilled which says, “Abraham believed God, and it was accounted to him as righteousness,” and he was called the friend of God.","canonicalTextHash":"ef0d5b960b22efcc50535c8c1a2d2ad463925f2e24b12001f3bf3ffc68f74db1","citation":"James 2:21–23","refId":"evidence:9dee981caab1a064da9c9ad0","referenceHash":"9dee981caab1a064da9c9ad064cdf9ad90608a1946ca4b60956875fd7e1a6b7e","sourceIds":["engwebu:jas:2:21-23"]}],"findings":[{"canonicalEvidence":"The